Read `AGENTS.md` first. It holds the shared project context: source of truth, layout, and the rules that hold everywhere. This file adds only how to work in this repository.

## Working discipline

- Implement one phase at a time, from `specs/01-product-spec.md` section 11. Do not start a phase that was not asked for, and do not build ahead.
- Never edit anything under `specs/` unless explicitly asked. When you find a gap or a contradiction in a specification, report it and stop; do not resolve it by choosing.
- Never edit `vendor/`, `node_modules/`, or lock files by hand.
- Prefer editing an existing file over creating a new one.
- Do not add a dependency without stating what it replaces and why the standard library or the framework is not enough.
- Tests belong in the same change as the code they cover, at the level `specs/06-testing.md` assigns them.

## When you are unsure

Say so. An answer of "the specification does not cover this" is correct and useful. A plausible invention is worse than a question, because it will be indistinguishable from a specified decision when it is reviewed.
